From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Liad Yosef <liad.yosef@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 23:48:30 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Read a shadow root's text content from its descendants

Node::text_content walked elements and anonymous blocks and skipped every
other kind, so it returned an empty string for a shadow root. A shadow
root is a DocumentFragment, whose textContent is the text of its
descendants, so ShadowRoot.textContent in the DOM shim read "" where
Chrome reads the text. The host's own text content is unchanged: the
root is not one of its children.
---
 src/node/node.rs | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/node/node.rs b/src/node/node.rs
index 2db7d94..4e76f9a 100644
--- a/src/node/node.rs
+++ b/src/node/node.rs
@@ -2771,7 +2771,8 @@ impl Node {
             NodeData::Text(data) => {
                 out.push_str(&data.content);
             }
-            NodeData::Element(..) | NodeData::AnonymousBlock(..) => {
+            // A shadow root is a DocumentFragment, whose textContent is its descendants' text.
+            NodeData::Element(..) | NodeData::AnonymousBlock(..) | NodeData::ShadowRoot(..) => {
                 for child_id in self.children().iter() {
                     self.with(child_id).write_text_content(out);
                 }
